# ── MediFlow Frontend — Environment / Configuration Reference ───────────────
#
# This is a vanilla-JS PWA with no build step.
# There is no .env file loaded automatically; instead, configure constants
# directly in app.js (or inject them via your hosting platform's build vars).
#
# ── Push Notifications (Web Push / VAPID) ───────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Generate a VAPID key pair on the backend:
#      npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#
# 2. On the BACKEND set these env vars:
#      VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=<your-public-key>
#      VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=<your-private-key>
#      VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@yourdomain.com
#
# 3. On the FRONTEND (app.js, line near the top):
#      const VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY = '<your-public-key>';
#    Replace 'YOUR_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE' with the public key from step 1.
#
# 4. Ensure the backend exposes:
#      POST /api/notifications/subscribe  — saves a PushSubscription object
#      POST /api/notifications/test       — sends a test push to the user
#
# 5. The service worker (sw.js) handles incoming push events automatically.
#    Notifications are displayed even when the browser tab is closed.
#
# ── Other Configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API_BASE and SOCKET_URL are also set at the top of app.js.
